@tradition tiles-night
// Tiles night (weekly, seat 15). Tuesday is the one evening with no other tradition, so Tiles has it to itself.
// The game itself is the Tiles engineer's (plans/tiles-plan.html, section 23); this file is only the gathering: who
// comes, where they sit, the boards on the tables, and the words. Design note: plans/trad-notes-weekly.md.
k: 435
title: Tiles night
when: weekly tuesday
at: 20:00-21:30
min: 25
jitter: 15
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
hold: 1
who: rina always, lounge-regular 60%, bar-regular 45%, juniors 35%, everyone 12%
anim: play
host: rina
from: rina
ties: decor tilesNight
ties: tally tiles-night
invite: host=rina odds=40% line="Tiles tonight in the lounge. Come and lose to me. It's educational."

== mail
- Tiles night tomorrow, {time} in the bow lounge. A board on every table. Beginners welcome; my title is not up for discussion.

== ask
- Tiles night later. I've been practising my losing face. Haven't needed it yet.   #funny
- Coming to Tiles tonight? There's a board with your name on it.
- Tiles at eight. Rina says it's a friendly game. Rina is lying.   #funny
- I'm playing Tiles tonight. Last week I nearly won. Nearly.

== here
- Your move. Take your time. No, really, take your time.   #funny
- Hang on, that tile goes there? Since when?
- One more game. Then bed. Probably.
- Good move. I hate it.   #funny

== thanks
- You pull up a chair at a Tiles board. The tiles click, the lounge hums, and someone groans at a good move.
- You join Tiles night. Rina looks up from the board and cracks her knuckles.   #funny

== chatter
- Has anyone actually beaten Rina at Tiles? Ever?   #funny
- I dreamt in Tiles last night. Little hexes everywhere.   #funny
- Tiles is easy to learn. That's the trap.
- Tuesday's the best night aboard. Tiles, tea, and nobody talking about work.   #warm
